msgid "Engage in a casual conversation with a friendly stranger at a social event. Perfect for practicing how to break the ice and keep the chat going naturally."
msgstr "Berbual secara santai dengan seorang yang tak dikenali di acara sosial. Sesuai untuk berlatih cara memecahkan kebuntuan dan memastikan perbualan berjalan lancar secara semula jadi."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/features/RolePlay/scenarios/small-talk-with-a-stranger.ts:13
msgid ""
"Talking to a stranger can feel uncomfortable because neither person knows what to say yet. The goal is not to sound especially clever or interesting. Your first goal is simply to make the other person feel comfortable and discover something you can talk about together.\n"
"\n"
"The advice below is inspired by ideas from Charles Duhigg’s book *Supercommunicators*.\n"
"\n"
"## How to Start a Conversation\n"
"\n"
"Use the situation you already share. You do not need an original or impressive opening line.\n"
"\n"
"Try making a simple observation and adding an easy question:\n"
"\n"
"- “This place is busier than I expected. Have you been here before?”\n"
"- “How do you know the host?”\n"
"- “What brought you to this event?”\n"
"- “That looks interesting. What are you drinking?”\n"
"- “Is this your first time at an event like this?”\n"
"\n"
"Questions about the immediate situation feel natural because they give the other person an obvious way to respond.\n"
"\n"
"## Ask Questions That Reveal More Than Facts\n"
"\n"
"Basic questions are useful for starting a conversation:\n"
"\n"
"- “Where are you from?”\n"
"- “What do you do?”\n"
"- “Do you live nearby?”\n"
"\n"
"However, a conversation becomes more interesting when you gently ask about the person’s experiences, feelings, or preferences.\n"
"\n"
"Instead of only asking:\n"
"\n"
"> “What do you do for work?”\n"
"\n"
"You could continue with:\n"
"\n"
"> “What do you enjoy most about it?”\n"
"\n"
"Instead of:\n"
"\n"
"> “How long have you lived here?”\n"
"\n"
"Try:\n"
"\n"
"> “What do you like most about living here?”\n"
"\n"
"Other useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “How did you become interested in that?”\n"
"- “What has been the best part of your week?”\n"
"- “What do you usually enjoy doing on weekends?”\n"
"- “What is something you are looking forward to?”\n"
"- “What kind of places do you like visiting?”\n"
"\n"
"These questions are personal enough to create a connection, but still safe and appropriate for someone you have just met.\n"
"\n"
"## Listen for the Kind of Conversation They Want\n"
"\n"
"People do not always want the same thing from a conversation. They may want to:\n"
"\n"
"1. Exchange information or make a decision.\n"
"2. Share an emotion or experience.\n"
"3. Talk about their interests, identity, or relationships.\n"
"\n"
"Try to respond to the kind of conversation the other person has started.\n"
"\n"
"If someone says:\n"
"\n"
"> “I moved here two weeks ago and everything still feels unfamiliar.”\n"
"\n"
"A purely practical response might be:\n"
"\n"
"> “You should download a city guide.”\n"
"\n"
"But an emotional response may connect better:\n"
"\n"
"> “That sounds exciting, but probably a little overwhelming too. How has it been so far?”\n"
"\n"
"You do not always need to solve a problem. Sometimes people simply want to feel understood.\n"
"\n"
"## Show That You Are Really Listening\n"
"\n"
"A useful technique is to:\n"
"\n"
"1. Ask a question.\n"
"2. Listen carefully.\n"
"3. Summarize the important part in your own words.\n"
"4. Check whether you understood correctly.\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"> “So you started learning photography because you wanted a creative hobby outside work. Did I understand that correctly?”\n"
"\n"
"You do not need to do this formally after every answer. Short natural responses also work:\n"
"\n"
"- “So that is what brought you here.”\n"
"- “It sounds like you really enjoyed it.”\n"
"- “I can see why that was frustrating.”\n"
"- “So you prefer quieter places?”\n"
"- “That makes sense.”\n"
"\n"
"These responses show that you are not simply waiting for your turn to speak.\n"
"\n"
"## Share Something About Yourself Too\n"
"\n"
"Good small talk should not feel like an interview. After asking a question, share a related detail about yourself.\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"> “What kind of music do you listen to? I’ve been listening to a lot of jazz recently, but I’m trying to discover something new.”\n"
"\n"
"Or:\n"
"\n"
"> “Have you travelled anywhere interesting recently? I visited a small town by a lake last weekend and really enjoyed it.”\n"
"\n"
"A useful pattern is:\n"
"\n"
"**Ask → Listen → Respond → Share → Ask again**\n"
"\n"
"This creates a balanced conversation in which both people gradually reveal more about themselves.\n"
"\n"
"## How to Keep the Conversation Going\n"
"\n"
"Listen for a detail you can explore.\n"
"\n"
"If the person says:\n"
"\n"
"> “I recently started running.”\n"
"\n"
"You could ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “What made you start?”\n"
"- “Do you prefer running alone or with other people?”\n"
"- “Was it difficult in the beginning?”\n"
"- “Are you training for anything?”\n"
"\n"
"You do not need to introduce a completely new topic after every answer. Often, the easiest way to continue is to become curious about one detail the person has already mentioned.\n"
"\n"
"## What to Avoid\n"
"\n"
"Try not to:\n"
"\n"
"- Ask many unrelated questions one after another.\n"
"- Turn every answer back to yourself.\n"
"- Give advice before understanding what the person needs.\n"
"- Ask questions that are too personal too quickly.\n"
"- Pretend to understand when you are confused.\n"
"- Focus so much on perfect grammar that you stop listening.\n"
"\n"
"It is completely natural to pause, search for a word, or ask someone to repeat themselves.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Sorry, could you say that again?”\n"
"- “What do you mean by that?”\n"
"- “I’m not sure I understood correctly.”\n"
"- “How would you describe it?”\n"
"- “Give me a second—I’m trying to find the right word.”\n"
"\n"
"## How to End the Conversation Politely\n"
"\n"
"Not every conversation needs to last a long time. You can finish warmly without making the moment awkward:\n"
"\n"
"- “It was really nice talking to you.”\n"
"- “I’m going to get another drink, but I’m glad we met.”\n"
"- “I’ll let you talk to the others, but I enjoyed our conversation.”\n"
"- “I hope you enjoy the rest of the event.”\n"
"- “Maybe I’ll see you again later.”\n"
"\n"
"Ending a conversation politely is also an important communication skill.\n"
"\n"
"## A Simple Conversation Formula\n"
"\n"
"When you are unsure what to do, remember:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Open:** Comment on the shared situation.\n"
"2. **Explore:** Ask about an experience, preference, or feeling.\n"
"3. **Listen:** Respond to something specific they said.\n"
"4. **Connect:** Share a related detail about yourself.\n"
"5. **Continue or close:** Ask a follow-up question or end politely.\n"
"\n"
"## Practice Scenario\n"
"\n"
"In this roleplay, you are meeting a friendly stranger at a social event. Start with an easy question, listen for interesting details, and gradually move from basic facts to experiences and interests.\n"
"\n"
"Try to practice at least three skills:\n"
"\n"
"- Ask one question about an experience or feeling.\n"
"- Refer to something the stranger said earlier.\n"
"- Share something related about yourself.\n"
"\n"
"Do not worry about creating a perfect conversation. Concentrate on being curious, attentive, and easy to talk to."
msgstr ""
"Berbual dengan orang asing boleh terasa janggal kerana kedua-duanya belum tahu apa yang perlu diperkatakan. Matlamatnya bukan untuk kedengaran terlalu bijak atau menarik. Matlamat pertama anda hanyalah untuk membuat orang lain merasa selesa dan menemui sesuatu yang boleh dibincangkan bersama.\n"
"\n"
"Nasihat di bawah ini diilhamkan oleh idea-idea daripada buku Charles Duhigg *Supercommunicators*.\n"
"\n"
"## Cara Memulakan Perbualan\n"
"\n"
"Gunakan situasi yang anda sudah kongsikan. Anda tidak memerlukan ayat pembukaan yang asli atau mengagumkan.\n"
"\n"
"Cuba buat pemerhatian ringkas dan tambahkan soalan mudah:\n"
"\n"
"- “Tempat ini lebih sibuk dari yang saya jangkakan. Pernahkah anda ke sini sebelum ini?”\n"
"- “Bagaimana anda kenal pengacara?”\n"
"- “Apa yang membawa anda ke acara ini?”\n"
"- “Itu nampak menarik. Apa yang anda minum?”\n"
"- “Adakah ini kali pertama anda di acara seperti ini?”\n"
"\n"
"Soalan tentang situasi semasa terasa alami kerana memberi orang lain cara yang jelas untuk menjawab.\n"
"\n"
"## Tanya Soalan Yang Mendedahkan Lebih Daripada Fakta\n"
"\n"
"Soalan asas berguna untuk memulakan perbualan:\n"
"\n"
"- “Dari mana asal anda?”\n"
"- “Apa yang anda lakukan?”\n"
"- “Adakah anda tinggal berhampiran?”\n"
"\n"
"Bagaimanapun, perbualan menjadi lebih menarik apabila anda dengan lembut bertanya tentang pengalaman, perasaan, atau keutamaan seseorang.\n"
"\n"
"Daripada hanya bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"> “Apa yang anda lakukan untuk bekerja?”\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh meneruskan dengan:\n"
"\n"
"> “Apa yang paling anda nikmati tentangnya?”\n"
"\n"
"Daripada bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"> “Berapa lama anda tinggal di sini?”\n"
"\n"
"Cuba:\n"
"\n"
"> “Apa yang paling anda suka tentang tinggal di sini?”\n"
"\n"
"Soalan lain yang berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- “Bagaimana anda mula berminat dalam itu?”\n"
"- “Apa bahagian terbaik dalam minggu anda?”\n"
"- “Apa yang biasanya anda suka lakukan pada hujung minggu?”\n"
"- “Apakah sesuatu yang anda nanti-nantikan?”\n"
"- “Jenis tempat apa yang anda suka lawati?”\n"
"\n"
"Soalan-soalan ini cukup peribadi untuk mewujudkan hubungan, tetapi masih selamat dan sesuai untuk seseorang yang baru anda kenali.\n"
"\n"
"## Dengar Jenis Perbualan Yang Mereka Inginkan\n"
"\n"
"Orang tidak selalu mahukan perkara yang sama dari perbualan. Mereka mungkin ingin:\n"
"\n"
"1. Berkongsi maklumat atau membuat keputusan.\n"
"2. Berkongsi emosi atau pengalaman.\n"
"3. Membincangkan minat, identiti, atau hubungan mereka.\n"
"\n"
"Cuba respons pada jenis perbualan yang telah dimulakan oleh orang lain.\n"
"\n"
"Jika seseorang berkata:\n"
"\n"
"> “Saya berpindah ke sini dua minggu lalu dan semuanya masih terasa asing.”\n"
"\n"
"Respons praktikal sepenuhnya mungkin:\n"
"\n"
"> “Anda patut memuat turun panduan bandar.”\n"
"\n"
"Tetapi respons emosional mungkin lebih menghubungkan:\n"
"\n"
"> “Kedengaran menyeronokkan, tetapi mungkin juga sedikit menakutkan. Bagaimana setakat ini?”\n"
"\n"
"Anda tidak selalu perlu menyelesaikan masalah. Kadang-kadang orang hanya mahu merasa difahami.\n"
"\n"
"## Tunjukkan Bahawa Anda Benar-Benar Mendengar\n"
"\n"
"Teknik yang berguna adalah untuk:\n"
"\n"
"1. Tanya soalan.\n"
"2. Dengar dengan teliti.\n"
"3. Ringkaskan bahagian penting dengan kata-kata anda sendiri.\n"
"4. Periksa sama ada anda faham dengan betul.\n"
"\n"
"Sebagai contoh:\n"
"\n"
"> “Jadi anda mula belajar fotografi kerana anda mahu hobi kreatif di luar kerja. Adakah saya faham dengan betul?”\n"
"\n"
"Anda tidak perlu melakukannya secara formal selepas setiap jawapan. Respons semula jadi yang ringkas juga berfungsi:\n"
"\n"
"- “Jadi itulah yang membawa anda ke sini.”\n"
"- “Nampaknya anda benar-benar menikmatinya.”\n"
"- “Saya boleh lihat mengapa ia mengecewakan.”\n"
"- “Jadi anda lebih suka tempat-tempat yang lebih tenang?”\n"
"- “Itu masuk akal.”\n"
"\n"
"Respons ini menunjukkan bahawa anda bukan sekadar menunggu giliran anda untuk bercakap.\n"
"\n"
"## Kongsi Sesuatu Tentang Diri Anda Juga\n"
"\n"
"Bual mesra yang baik tidak sepatutnya terasa seperti temubual. Selepas bertanya soalan, kongsi maklumat berkaitan tentang diri anda.\n"
"\n"
"Sebagai contoh:\n"
"\n"
"> “Jenis muzik apa yang anda dengar? Saya banyak mendengar jazz akhir-akhir ini, tetapi saya cuba untuk menemui sesuatu yang baru.”\n"
"\n"
"Atau:\n"
"\n"
"> “Adakah anda pernah melancong ke tempat menarik baru-baru ini? Saya melawat sebuah bandar kecil di tepi tasik minggu lalu dan sangat menikmatinya.”\n"
"\n"
"Corak yang berguna adalah:\n"
"\n"
"**Tanya → Dengar → Respons → Kongsi → Tanya semula**\n"
"\n"
"Ini mewujudkan perbualan seimbang di mana kedua-dua orang secara beransur-ansur mendedahkan lebih banyak tentang diri mereka.\n"
"\n"
"## Cara Meneruskan Perbualan\n"
"\n"
"Dengar untuk butiran yang boleh anda terokai.\n"
"\n"
"Jika orang itu berkata:\n"
"\n"
"> “Saya baru mula berlari.”\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- “Apa yang membuatkan anda mula?”\n"
"- “Adakah anda lebih suka berlari sendirian atau dengan orang lain?”\n"
"- “Adakah ia sukar pada awalnya?”\n"
"- “Adakah anda sedang berlatih untuk sesuatu?”\n"
"\n"
"Anda tidak perlu memperkenalkan topik baru sepenuhnya selepas setiap jawapan. Selalunya, cara terbaik untuk meneruskan adalah menjadi ingin tahu tentang satu butiran yang orang itu telah sebutkan.\n"
"\n"
"## Apa Yang Perlu Dielakkan\n"
"\n"
"Cuba untuk tidak:\n"
"\n"
"- Menanyakan banyak soalan yang tidak berkaitan satu demi satu.\n"
"- Mengaitkan setiap jawapan kembali kepada diri anda.\n"
"- Memberi nasihat sebelum memahami apa yang diperlukan oleh orang itu.\n"
"- Menanya soalan yang terlalu peribadi terlalu cepat.\n"
"- Berpura-pura faham apabila anda keliru.\n"
"- Tumpu begitu banyak pada tatabahasa sempurna sehingga anda berhenti mendengar.\n"
"\n"
"Ia benar-benar semula jadi untuk berhenti sebentar, mencari perkataan, atau meminta seseorang mengulangi diri mereka.\n"
"\n"
"Frasa berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- “Maaf, bolehkah anda katakan semula?”\n"
"- “Apa maksud anda dengan itu?”\n"
"- “Saya tidak pasti saya faham dengan betul.”\n"
"- “Bagaimana anda akan menggambarkannya?”\n"
"- “Berikan saya sesaat—saya cuba mencari perkataan yang sesuai.”\n"
"\n"
"## Cara Mengakhiri Perbualan dengan Sopan\n"
"\n"
"Tidak setiap perbualan perlu berlangsung lama. Anda boleh mengakhirinya dengan mesra tanpa membuat saat itu canggung:\n"
"\n"
"- “Sangat gembira bercakap dengan anda.”\n"
"- “Saya akan ambil minuman lain, tetapi saya gembira kita bertemu.”\n"
"- “Saya akan biarkan anda bercakap dengan yang lain, tetapi saya menikmati perbualan kita.”\n"
"- “Saya harap anda menikmati acara selebihnya.”\n"
"- “Mungkin saya akan melihat anda lagi nanti.”\n"
"\n"
"Mengakhiri perbualan dengan sopan juga merupakan kemahiran komunikasi penting.\n"
"\n"
"## Formula Perbualan Mudah\n"
"\n"
"Apabila anda tidak pasti apa yang perlu dilakukan, ingatlah:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Buka:** Komen tentang situasi yang dikongsikan.\n"
"2. **Teroka:** Tanya tentang pengalaman, keutamaan, atau perasaan.\n"
"3. **Dengar:** Respons kepada sesuatu yang spesifik yang mereka katakan.\n"
"4. **Hubungkan:** Kongsi maklumat berkaitan tentang diri anda.\n"
"5. **Teruskan atau akhirkan:** Tanya soalan susulan atau tamatkan dengan sopan.\n"
"\n"
"## Skenario Latihan\n"
"\n"
"Dalam permainan peranan ini, anda bertemu dengan orang asing yang ramah di acara sosial. Mulakan dengan soalan mudah, dengar butiran menarik, dan secara beransur-ansur beralih dari fakta asas kepada pengalaman dan minat.\n"
"\n"
"Cuba praktikkan sekurang-kurangnya tiga kemahiran:\n"
"\n"
"- Tanya satu soalan tentang pengalaman atau perasaan.\n"
"- Rujuk kepada sesuatu yang telah disebutkan oleh orang asing itu sebelum ini.\n"
"- Kongsi sesuatu yang berkaitan tentang diri anda.\n"
"\n"
"Jangan risau tentang mencipta perbualan yang sempurna. Tumpukan pada menjadi ingin tahu, memberi perhatian, dan mudah berbual."

